{
  "definition": "A cell is the closed square [ox+128x, ox+128x+128] x [oy+128y, oy+128y+128] from the BLOCKMAP origin; a line meets it when its closed segment meets the closed square (inclusive bounding-box overlap, and the supporting line does not leave all four corners strictly on one side), in exact integers. Reading (a): the leading 0 word is the format's marker, not a listing. Reading (b): it is a listing of linedef 0, as P_BlockLinesIterator iterates it (p_maputl.c:493-504). Miss class: \"0\" when every listing meets its cell, \"1\" when every missing listing's line meets a cell within Chebyshev distance 1 of the listed cell, \"more than 1\" otherwise.",
